# Deploys web/ to GitHub Pages on every push to main.
#
# This file ends in .todo so GitHub ignores it. Rename it to deploy.yml once
# it's filled in. GitHub only runs .yml/.yaml files in this folder, and an
# unfinished one would fail on every push.
#
# Starting point: in repo Settings -> Pages, set Source to "GitHub Actions" and
# GitHub suggests a "Static HTML" starter workflow. It's close to what you
# need; read every line of it before using it.
#
# What this workflow needs to do:
#   1. Trigger: on push to main, plus workflow_dispatch so you can run it by hand.
#      Optional: only run when files under web/ change (a paths filter).
#   2. Permissions: contents: read, pages: write, id-token: write.
#   3. Steps:
#        - check out the repo
#        - configure Pages
#        - upload web/ as the Pages artifact   <- the starter uploads the whole
#                                                 repo; change the path to web/
#        - deploy the artifact
#
# Note: when you deploy with Actions, you set the custom domain in repo
# Settings -> Pages. A CNAME file in the site folder is ignored.
